                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.15659/2609.15659v1/figures/assets/fig_noise3d.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:KaiNinja pipeline.A frozen DINOv3 encoder conditions\nevery block of both stages through cross-attention.Stage 1, the\nlayout flow, denoises two 3D noise grids into per-volume occupancy layouts.\nEach stream has its own self-attention weights, and a shared zero-initialized\nglobal-attention block connects the streams every six blocks (×5\\times 5).Stage 2, the refinement flow, keeps the TRELLIS.2 weights and\ndenoises sparse noise on the active voxels (NAN_{A},NBN_{B}tokens) with two\nintra-volume blocks and one global block per group (×10\\times 10). Frozen\nVAEs decode the latents of both stages, and the two O-Voxel volumes are\nassembled into the part-separated mesh. No mask or segmenter appears in the\npipeline.",
